At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

We're looking for a Sr. Marketing Strategist &nbsp;to support the execution and operational excellence of marketing initiatives across FlixBus and Greyhound in North America (US &amp; Canada). Reporting to the Head of Marketing for North America, this role brings integrated marketing campaigns to life by coordinating cross-functional teams, managing marketing operations, overseeing brand governance, and ensuring consistent execution across all customer touchpoints. &nbsp;

About the Role

• Plan and support the end-to-end execution of integrated marketing campaigns across FlixBus and Greyhound, maintaining the North America campaign calendar and delivering post-campaign performance recaps. &nbsp;

• Execute North American CRM initiatives in partnership with the Global CRM team, coordinating briefs, localization, market-specific messaging, and ongoing performance optimization. &nbsp;

• Own day-to-day management of Greyhound North America social media operations - including agency partnership, social listening, trend monitoring, and channel performance reporting. &nbsp;

• Prepare and distribute weekly marketing updates, maintain project trackers and documentation libraries, and coordinate marketing requests across departments to keep workflows on track. &nbsp;

• Review marketing materials for brand consistency, coordinate creative approval workflows, and manage creative requests and briefs with Global Creative teams. &nbsp;

• Serve as the key liaison between North America Marketing and Global Marketing teams, coordinating meetings, project updates, and cross-functional stakeholder communications. &nbsp;

• Support new route launches, partnership activations, and regional marketing initiatives, ensuring all deliverables remain aligned with business priorities and launch timelines. &nbsp;

About You

• Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Communications or a related field.&nbsp;

• Strong understanding of CRM, social media, and integrated campaign execution across multiple channels. &nbsp;

• Exceptional project management and organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. &nbsp;

• Proven experience working with creative teams and agency partners to deliver high-quality marketing assets. &nbsp;

• Analytical mindset with experience building campaign reporting frameworks and translating data into actionable insights. &nbsp;

• Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to influence and align cross-functional stakeholders. &nbsp;

• Highly collaborative, comfortable working across multiple business functions; familiarity with project management and marketing collaboration tools is a plus. &nbsp;

• Willingness to travel, up to 25% of time.

Salary range: $110,000 - $120,000 USD&nbsp;

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

